Privacy Policy
Effective date: August 29, 2025
This Privacy Policy describes how Roman’s APP (the “Service”), operating via the Facebook Page CodeWave, collects, uses, and shares information when you interact with our Messenger bot on Meta/Facebook (the “Platform”).

1) Who we are
Controller: Roman’s APP / CodeWave (Messenger bot)
Contact: privacy@yourdomain.com

2) Information we collect
Conversation content: Messages you send to the bot and our replies, including attachments you choose to send (e.g., images).
Identifiers: Page-Scoped ID (PSID) and basic profile metadata provided by the Platform (e.g., name, profile link/picture if available).
Technical and delivery data: Timestamps, delivery/read events, and event types required to operate the bot.
Diagnostics/analytics (if enabled): Aggregated metrics to improve quality and reliability.
3) How we use information
Provide, maintain, and improve the bot’s functionality and respond to requests.
Monitor for abuse, security, and compliance with Meta policies and our terms.
Debugging, analytics, and quality assurance.
4) Legal bases (EEA/UK users)
Where applicable, we rely on one or more of: performance of a contract, legitimate interests (to provide and secure the Service), and consent where required.

5) Sharing of information
We do not sell personal information. We may share limited data with trusted service providers (e.g., hosting, workflow automation, analytics) under appropriate confidentiality and data-processing terms. We may disclose information if required by law or to protect rights, privacy, safety, or property.

6) Data retention
We retain conversation logs and related metadata only as long as necessary for the purposes above, or as required by law. If you stop interacting with the bot, we periodically review and delete older data that is no longer needed.

7) Security
We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect personal information. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure.

8) Children’s privacy
The Service is not directed to children under 13 (or the equivalent age in your jurisdiction). If we learn that a child has provided personal information, we will take reasonable steps to delete it.

9) International transfers
Your information may be processed and stored in countries other than your own. Where required, we implement appropriate safeguards for such transfers.

10) Your rights
Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict the use of your personal information, as well as rights to object and data portability. To exercise these rights, contact us at privacy@yourdomain.com.

11) Third‑party services
Our bot uses the Meta (Facebook) Messenger Platform and may integrate with workflow/automation tools (e.g., n8n) or hosting providers. Your use of Meta’s services is subject to Meta’s own terms and policies.

12) Changes to this Policy
We may update this Policy from time to time. The “Effective date” above indicates the latest revision. Material changes will be communicated by updating this page.

13) Contact
Questions or concerns? Email us at privacy@yourdomain.com.

